values ('c6f2a8d1-4b37-4e09-9a15-2d0e7c5b6f18', 'u-s-health-care-system', 'U.S. Health Care System', 'A first- or second-year core course introducing how the United States finances, organizes, regulates, delivers, measures, and reforms health care. Students learn to trace a person''s path through coverage and care, read health-system data, identify institutional incentives, analyze inequities, compare the United States with peer systems, and evaluate reform proposals using explicit goals and tradeoffs.');

