  'U.S. Health Care System',
  'A first- or second-year core course introducing how the United States finances, organizes, regulates, delivers, measures, and reforms health care. Students learn to trace a person''s path through coverage and care, read health-system data, identify institutional incentives, analyze inequities, compare the United States with peer systems, and evaluate reform proposals using explicit goals and tradeoffs.',
  $ushcsjson${"slug": "u-s-health-care-system", "title": "U.S. Health Care System", "description": "A first- or second-year core course introducing how the United States finances, organizes, regulates, delivers, measures, and reforms health care. Students learn to trace a person's path through coverage and care, read health-system data, identify institutional incentives, analyze inequities, compare the United States with peer systems, and evaluate reform proposals using explicit goals and tradeoffs.", "topics": [{"id": "05087417-5dfa-4de7-b5a9-ba686c370c66", "type": "topic", "title": "Origins, Values, and Structure of the U.S. Health Care System", "description": "Explains how history, federalism, markets, professional institutions, and contested values produced a fragmented mix of public and private organizations.", "children": [{"id": "7fe9e0bc-276b-4256-bd2f-e21fcb342fb7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical development", "description": "The system is easier to understand as layered policy choices than as a single design.", "children": [{"id": "d2397050-b29b-4368-9040-71d9985c9429", "type": "concept", "title": "Professionalization and hospital growth"}, {"id": "b154d46e-42ed-492e-be61-931ce3c776a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Employment-based insurance and tax policy"}, {"id": "228d3a42-d8bc-4db9-98e4-db3c786bb937", "type": "concept", "title": "Creation of Medicare and Medicaid"}, {"id": "963f40f7-941c-4b44-9b17-4fa4b2cfc005", "type": "concept", "title": "Managed care, ACA, and contemporary consolidation"}]}, {"id": "cc21f81a-a3c7-4ea5-80ef-af4a1460911a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Organizational structure", "description": "Students identify the institutions that finance, organize, deliver, regulate, and receive care.", "children": [{"id": "630cdaab-07a0-4f83-95ae-922330ca3b31", "type": "concept", "title": "Patients, families, and communities"}, {"id": "63461520-1aeb-444b-b494-05983636f2e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Purchasers, payers, and intermediaries"}, {"id": "6ba63017-e202-4d6e-afb0-8fbb96ffb452", "type": "concept", "title": "Providers, suppliers, and systems"}, {"id": "7456afb3-2b2a-4f0e-b4c7-ffc6b9d1817f", "type": "concept", "title": "Regulators, accreditors, and public-health agencies"}]}, {"id": "7dbde7ec-8190-4483-a6b0-3431a5700c93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Values and goals", "description": "System debates reflect competing views of health care as a right, good, service, investment, and public responsibility.", "children": [{"id": "6bc496ab-df73-44f3-b908-452004b814d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Access and universality"}, {"id": "b935bf6c-bca1-4c55-92d1-4a17e22768bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality and safety"}, {"id": "37b181a0-c110-437e-a827-3db4ca3e2140", "type": "concept", "title": "Efficiency and affordability"}, {"id": "4d0556b8-7281-4037-a288-60ac92534722", "type": "concept", "title": "Choice, equity, solidarity, and innovation"}]}]}, {"id": "5e04c5d1-2e97-4d96-bf1e-19616764c703", "type": "topic", "title": "Government Roles, Regulation, and Health Policy Institutions", "description": "Maps federal, state, local, tribal, and territorial authority and the agencies, legislatures, courts, and interest groups that shape health-system rules.", "children": [{"id": "12201ef0-cdbb-4790-b9ef-96928399080d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Federalism", "description": "Authority is distributed across levels of government, creating variation and coordination problems.", "children": [{"id": "0e5385e3-0e53-4c5a-b49c-ef5da7cd4d10", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal powers and financing"}, {"id": "6a73efe5-82b1-491e-9004-e3f0f35c18ee", "type": "concept", "title": "State insurance, professional, and facility regulation"}, {"id": "30fdb3ee-0875-4f45-9542-c63004893f8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Local delivery and public health"}, {"id": "cf33c235-9374-4381-a747-b6ff50175773", "type": "concept", "title": "Tribal sovereignty and territorial systems"}]}, {"id": "9c9ebb6e-74be-4967-ab70-88f5a73cd3e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and agencies", "description": "Students learn which bodies make, administer, interpret, and evaluate policy.", "children": [{"id": "f45fb0e1-81bd-46ac-9ade-bfd2e8873a6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Congress, executive branch, and courts"}, {"id": "65d73a4f-ca24-4d47-9b9a-85e0db2f428c", "type": "concept", "title": "HHS, CMS, CDC, FDA, HRSA, AHRQ, and NIH"}, {"id": "0c8f28c6-82ec-44fa-8e51-15f661c08933", "type": "concept", "title": "State agencies and insurance departments"}, {"id": "fbaf9096-0f6c-4712-bd09-2e8b602c1d17", "type": "concept", "title": "Independent commissions and advisory bodies"}]}, {"id": "ef9e3378-9a39-489f-836f-41561bddc97b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy process and influence", "description": "Formal authority interacts with organized interests, evidence, budgets, and public opinion.", "children": [{"id": "62ed3469-d75e-4e56-9a7b-9b9cb2e48c15", "type": "concept", "title": "Legislation and regulation"}, {"id": "7a149052-551b-48c0-acb8-8ebb23fbaff6", "type": "concept", "title": "Waivers and demonstrations"}, {"id": "38f15005-fb28-4f03-a955-976e39f5b198", "type": "concept", "title": "Litigation and judicial review"}, {"id": "637343fc-2af7-429a-94da-56abf9fe4189", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest groups, lobbying, advocacy, and media"}]}]}, {"id": "d9379ac3-d41f-482c-b83b-4f643b5ec38a", "type": "topic", "title": "Public and Private Financing", "description": "Shows where the health dollar comes from, how risk is pooled, who pays, and how taxes, premiums, cost sharing, and uncompensated care distribute burdens.", "children": [{"id": "e6c15520-49dd-4f1f-8411-0b15132b5311", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sources of funds", "description": "Health care is financed through taxes, premiums, household payments, and cross-subsidies.", "children": [{"id": "17a91ce0-8921-4b71-ad21-81a80ae02779", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal, state, and local revenues"}, {"id": "d9e5f128-0c79-43c1-ae85-0dc8437a3239", "type": "concept", "title": "Employer and employee premiums"}, {"id": "67044ba1-da4c-49f3-83e4-ae4e6e50d3f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual premiums and cost sharing"}, {"id": "0b33ff3f-eaae-461d-972a-d6316506cf24", "type": "concept", "title": "Uncompensated care and charitable support"}]}, {"id": "aec39140-db81-4182-b96e-74c1e48b70f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk pooling", "description": "Pooling spreads uncertain costs, but enrollment and benefit rules distribute risk differently.", "children": [{"id": "df649da3-69f0-41bc-9d92-ea480e3e12dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk, adverse selection, and moral hazard"}, {"id": "80980110-5448-45b5-a620-26c037c532d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Community and experience rating"}, {"id": "4a19e2f2-f893-441f-b5a3-a510447bc001", "type": "concept", "title": "Reinsurance and risk adjustment"}, {"id": "4b8aafd4-c5b8-4254-88f2-255ccd61b87b", "type": "concept", "title": "Pooling size and fragmentation"}]}, {"id": "c930a90c-121f-4d81-8f03-aaae5d7bc75f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Incidence and burden", "description": "Who writes the check is not always who ultimately bears the cost.", "children": [{"id": "9e5b0eac-6f2a-4b5e-a200-828128470541", "type": "concept", "title": "Wage tradeoffs"}, {"id": "9bf222cb-d981-445a-945d-bfff5392e234", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax incidence"}, {"id": "ff982971-1ae3-4f77-ab80-cfe3975304e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Premium and out-of-pocket burden"}, {"id": "8912e6d4-0b20-4e98-8e34-9e8dbc6d9785", "type": "concept", "title": "Regressive and progressive financing"}]}]}, {"id": "74227c2f-9007-403c-8af6-a1587d407eba", "type": "topic", "title": "Medicare, Medicaid, CHIP, and the Affordable Care Act", "description": "Compares eligibility, benefits, administration, financing, delivery arrangements, and current policy tensions across major public coverage programs.", "children": [{"id": "a186cde3-81b4-40ab-bb29-b89526ba6c3f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Medicare", "description": "Medicare is a federal social insurance program with distinct parts, benefits, payment systems, and supplemental coverage.", "children": [{"id": "f42a994e-ae15-4102-8d35-b5a23b49132a", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility and Parts A–D"}, {"id": "d00e02a1-ab91-42d0-b541-32e6be3d21dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Traditional Medicare and Medicare Advantage"}, {"id": "607c1128-b516-4d82-a24d-938574cc6086", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost sharing and supplemental coverage"}, {"id": "cef524f3-5644-4af8-8254-dc05f4f9ac0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Payment, solvency, and access issues"}]}, {"id": "54e32c89-53ff-4383-abf8-124328b34672", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Medicaid and CHIP", "description": "These federal–state programs vary substantially in eligibility, benefits, delivery, and payment.", "children": [{"id": "89bcbbeb-c691-44ba-b48a-b06786d5bf34", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility categories and expansion"}, {"id": "98547ace-1b0f-4141-9e1a-b18de94b00b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal matching and state administration"}, {"id": "789b08de-7905-4e43-89a4-859efc168edf", "type": "concept", "title": "Managed care and fee-for-service"}, {"id": "c1b233ac-6802-4dcb-b2fe-b043c6df9cf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Children, disability, long-term services, and waivers"}]}, {"id": "2f27a3bb-0ee3-4fa9-8ce2-19c8d27ba706", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Affordable Care Act", "description": "The ACA reshaped individual coverage, insurance rules, Medicaid eligibility, and delivery reform.", "children": [{"id": "db985464-de01-401c-b42b-a59d2cdcaa2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Marketplaces and subsidies"}, {"id": "1c558bbd-8ef5-4768-9b8c-23b03459c2b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer protections"}, {"id": "04946c08-1cad-4d06-be02-4fe1024f7e36", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual and employer provisions"}, {"id": "41976b7c-74aa-4eff-a69f-06438559835b", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage gains, remaining gaps, and state variation"}]}]}, {"id": "91155c9f-bfc7-4e42-a25e-6b935c81e71b", "type": "topic", "title": "Private Insurance, Employer Coverage, and Managed Care", "description": "Examines benefit design, networks, utilization management, risk selection, employer sponsorship, marketplaces, and the patient experience of using insurance.", "children": [{"id": "a65082c3-ee16-499c-baf0-85b9a35ed105", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Employer-sponsored insurance", "description": "Employment remains a major coverage pathway shaped by tax policy, firm decisions, and labor markets.", "children": [{"id": "03e99923-a185-47f1-9778-5eb04508eca3", "type": "concept", "title": "Fully insured and self-funded plans"}, {"id": "36b3c548-e0a4-45c9-a5c9-50bc1c7472d0", "type": "concept", "title": "ERISA context"}, {"id": "abfe16f3-518f-4f69-9c8e-ca5962cda638", "type": "concept", "title": "Premium contributions and benefit design"}, {"id": "db6ed7fe-8a79-4970-b84c-edec1b1f5a87", "type": "concept", "title": "Job changes, COBRA, and portability"}]}, {"id": "54a3868e-a7ea-4dea-9216-dc1c223413ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plan design", "description": "Insurance terms translate directly into affordability and access.", "children": [{"id": "36ce7b9a-a76c-4db1-9522-4a1e4e32bdc9", "type": "concept", "title": "Premium, deductible, copayment, and coinsurance"}, {"id": "9a466285-5e4f-4c36-addb-742044e36f68", "type": "concept", "title": "Out-of-pocket maximum"}, {"id": "7deb45c3-7be2-4682-88ac-114636c8c91a", "type": "concept", "title": "Covered benefits and exclusions"}, {"id": "0a368511-1f60-46cb-8927-1c80eb6e4aa1", "type": "concept", "title": "Formularies, tiers, and prior authorization"}]}, {"id": "06ccbebd-e410-4cea-a89a-f862c6380ec8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Managed care", "description": "Managed care coordinates financing and delivery through networks and utilization tools.", "children": [{"id": "09535ee8-01c1-4259-9d92-ec047adecf4e", "type": "concept", "title": "HMO, PPO, EPO, and POS models"}, {"id": "954547da-e354-4a90-b365-8033db5e7dc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Networks and referrals"}, {"id": "ce03c693-0ef2-4fe1-ac32-2f46364dd6fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Utilization management"}, {"id": "10c320c2-d174-45ce-adf4-2dce21aa9159", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk adjustment, selection, and consumer protection"}]}]}, {"id": "77f5f834-0aef-4628-a9b4-b396fd9bcbc4", "type": "topic", "title": "Health Care Spending, Prices, Payment, and Incentives", "description": "Connects national spending and prices to fee-for-service, prospective payment, capitation, value-based payment, consolidation, and provider behavior.", "children": [{"id": "0160529a-b51a-4f08-a2bc-0ca1bb61143a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spending measurement", "description": "Students distinguish national totals, per-person spending, growth, price, volume, intensity, and administrative cost.", "children": [{"id": "61050393-5edf-466f-8cba-4a472f02483c", "type": "concept", "title": "National Health Expenditure Accounts"}, {"id": "244822f5-06c8-4d64-8a4c-a3fb63d3f779", "type": "concept", "title": "Payer and service categories"}, {"id": "ee6a3794-5aaa-401e-97f3-a03860b06877", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal, real, and share-of-GDP measures"}, {"id": "63092caf-99fc-46ac-8b2f-c1667c4898cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical versus projected spending"}]}, {"id": "1ddc94cb-6c26-4132-ad4c-fb321ecb9537", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Provider payment", "description": "Payment units and risk allocation shape service volume, coordination, coding, and investment.", "children": [{"id": "6dc3a79a-613c-4c2e-bea5-6e4c93cfb660", "type": "concept", "title": "Fee-for-service"}, {"id": "a2ac5662-f266-4681-8ca2-41b8a73c56f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Prospective and diagnosis-related payment"}, {"id": "1cee8090-3660-480a-a95f-e745cd0ad1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Bundled payment and shared savings"}, {"id": "75605e2b-bf0c-478d-ac59-ca6b86df91e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Capitation and global budgets"}]}, {"id": "649782e5-3137-4dd4-8cf2-f537ea51dbf9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prices and market power", "description": "High prices can reflect bargaining leverage, consolidation, regulation, input cost, and benefit design.", "children": [{"id": "aa5101d5-faa1-45d5-a59b-8b85e02cf879", "type": "concept", "title": "Commercial and administered prices"}, {"id": "de95654f-27a6-49c2-86d5-9b6b827a3559", "type": "concept", "title": "Hospital and physician consolidation"}, {"id": "326028b1-c83d-4ad0-b529-c4ed351cecf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiated rates and transparency"}, {"id": "c2dedb42-e710-4f7c-81a0-423babbadde9", "type": "concept", "title": "Competition policy and rate regulation"}]}]}, {"id": "f7539338-2a28-4f36-9013-863262618415", "type": "topic", "title": "Hospitals, Physicians, and Ambulatory Care", "description": "Describes how care is organized across hospitals, medical groups, community health centers, retail and virtual settings, and increasingly consolidated systems.", "children": [{"id": "03b3b3d2-aa5d-43ab-ad99-568f726ef2d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hospitals and health systems", "description": "Hospitals combine clinical, emergency, teaching, business, and community functions.", "children": [{"id": "85926be4-5980-4b8f-bfdf-d1fee7291c4c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ownership and tax status"}, {"id": "a61c660e-2e8a-44b4-84a9-18e91f888778", "type": "concept", "title": "Service lines and levels of care"}, {"id": "398bfd57-4bd3-401e-bd3b-dd05c3ab7512", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic, safety-net, rural, and specialty hospitals"}, {"id": "a94c93a9-7162-4316-a654-af7fac1efb67", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration, consolidation, and community benefit"}]}, {"id": "330c3f9c-c355-4058-9da9-dccb55a2a486", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Physician organization", "description": "Practice structure affects autonomy, access, coordination, and payment.", "children": [{"id": "a9828020-214a-4ed1-a556-8aa7e956bf73", "type": "concept", "title": "Independent and employed practice"}, {"id": "c88fc205-5c2b-407c-8bab-390b515cdc3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical groups and integrated systems"}, {"id": "2d938ec0-bb52-4e6a-98d1-a489e061bea3", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and specialty care"}, {"id": "cd62ddde-3759-4a91-a6a9-abcb68b860fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Referral relationships and accountable care"}]}, {"id": "cfb3ca2e-0861-4f30-9685-33d9f6d9d0fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ambulatory transformation", "description": "Care increasingly occurs outside the hospital through new settings and delivery models.", "children": [{"id": "3952a0d7-3599-43b1-878e-82ef5b1dbce9", "type": "concept", "title": "Community health centers"}, {"id": "1c2fcfc9-7a4d-42a1-9629-e2dc6bf6dabb", "type": "concept", "title": "Urgent, retail, and home-based care"}, {"id": "dabae026-eaed-4cdf-9aff-eae8c5d19711", "type": "concept", "title": "Telehealth and digital care"}, {"id": "03cf7b23-4c20-42da-ba3c-c55918713abc", "type": "concept", "title": "Hospital-at-home and site-neutral policy"}]}]}, {"id": "db60fc24-6103-4f04-ad07-76169e426ce2", "type": "topic", "title": "Health Workforce and Professional Practice", "description": "Analyzes workforce supply, distribution, training, scope, teams, labor conditions, burnout, and the structural causes of shortages and maldistribution.", "children": [{"id": "8fa79ce0-ce83-43c3-9019-6f3d21dd788e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply and distribution", "description": "National headcounts can conceal shortages by geography, specialty, population, and setting.", "children": [{"id": "b7eea2ca-0431-41ba-9655-689c59c164a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Training pipeline and graduate education"}, {"id": "dfaba387-8de6-4296-9b2c-ea4cc2bd9968", "type": "concept", "title": "Licensure and scope of practice"}, {"id": "a932d346-d2d2-4970-9bf7-483f3671667b", "type": "concept", "title": "Health professional shortage areas"}, {"id": "3e2d3721-36a1-4662-9e27-8910089fba13", "type": "concept", "title": "Rural and underserved distribution"}]}, {"id": "f13219e9-ede7-4018-8f6f-ea04925acbe4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Teams and roles", "description": "Modern care depends on coordination across professions and community workers.", "children": [{"id": "ed1159e2-cb7a-4fa6-aa2d-bae878024267", "type": "concept", "title": "Physicians, nurses, advanced practice clinicians"}, {"id": "1138dc2d-8440-466c-90c7-12a5268ac752", "type": "concept", "title": "Allied health, pharmacy, behavioral health, and oral health"}, {"id": "61c56498-13b2-4a76-bdba-f2affed14a67", "type": "concept", "title": "Community health workers and peer support"}, {"id": "de6c8d3e-3367-4559-bad1-b070baf08920", "type": "concept", "title": "Team-based and interprofessional care"}]}, {"id": "834da021-e0f5-42dd-b930-30ebaccb6e95", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Work conditions", "description": "Labor markets and organizational environments affect capacity, safety, retention, and equity.", "children": [{"id": "56eb1a0f-15f7-4287-aaf1-358e970da471", "type": "concept", "title": "Compensation and productivity"}, {"id": "38b945a8-41d7-49ef-8c02-c6b64e9504d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Burnout, moral distress, and turnover"}, {"id": "4a6ac41f-f63e-4fe7-89f1-21593ca7b1e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Unionization and staffing policy"}, {"id": "bc641722-ad1f-4001-9a66-da356148d5b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Diversity, inclusion, and career pathways"}]}]}, {"id": "1d25f155-8af6-41ac-a5c7-93b11a60d190", "type": "topic", "title": "Pharmaceuticals, Devices, and Health Technology", "description": "Follows innovation from research and regulation through pricing, coverage, prescribing, safety surveillance, access, and evidence of comparative value.", "children": [{"id": "6fe3cca8-6f58-4e57-b905-1827b699709e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Innovation pathway", "description": "Products move from discovery through trials, regulation, manufacturing, adoption, and surveillance.", "children": [{"id": "1a26e3a5-0993-4a14-8294-94355eebf831", "type": "concept", "title": "Research and development"}, {"id": "647295c4-6ef8-4284-92c6-d8f0aa5bd4cf", "type": "concept", "title": "FDA approval and evidence standards"}, {"id": "9e8bd908-332c-4001-9d53-9190bacf6411", "type": "concept", "title": "Patents, exclusivity, and competition"}, {"id": "f4e63c34-6400-456f-8351-5cd4ab10b14b", "type": "concept", "title": "Postmarket safety and recalls"}]}, {"id": "f9a94dad-08ec-4793-ac68-61ee0b7deb40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pricing and coverage", "description": "List price, net price, benefit design, rebates, and purchasing rules shape access and spending.", "children": [{"id": "8dcad834-28d9-4a80-9fba-6a3b775b67a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Manufacturers, wholesalers, pharmacies, and PBMs"}, {"id": "da3b7fea-f5e4-4d29-acc6-a660f12a9f1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Formularies and utilization management"}, {"id": "21e4eceb-576f-44b4-bc41-7537ba19daa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Generic and biosimilar competition"}, {"id": "9349cad9-8afd-48c8-a1de-122b0bac25f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiation, inflation controls, and assistance programs"}]}, {"id": "b5f8eb29-7675-4281-98a4-0c8e89aa71b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Technology assessment", "description": "Innovation should be evaluated for outcomes, harms, cost, equity, and opportunity cost.", "children": [{"id": "3c3646e4-e126-4675-8a64-4885d65e80ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative effectiveness"}, {"id": "a28fc2bf-4218-4338-aa57-cc468e69e803", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-effectiveness and budget impact"}, {"id": "31de6832-b6d8-43b7-8dd6-6e38b176e167", "type": "concept", "title": "Diffusion and low-value care"}, {"id": "e3bddbd6-0532-4910-9139-7719554688f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital health, algorithms, and evidence gaps"}]}]}, {"id": "cc89ebea-5856-4aeb-95cc-aa4082df796e", "type": "topic", "title": "Behavioral Health, Long-Term Services, and Post-Acute Care", "description": "Brings often-separated systems into view, including mental health, substance use, disability supports, home care, nursing facilities, rehabilitation, and family caregiving.", "children": [{"id": "80b0b767-9225-4ddd-a60c-4ff3b5a2fb20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Behavioral health", "description": "Financing and delivery remain fragmented despite parity and integration efforts.", "children": [{"id": "2ad186e7-e9bc-42d3-b3b3-1951f4afbcb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental health and substance-use services"}, {"id": "46b5948a-5541-4db9-b690-4a9c56848a79", "type": "concept", "title": "Parity and coverage"}, {"id": "88c48052-43aa-473c-98f8-297dd9f61a9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Crisis systems and emergency care"}, {"id": "c2a95ffd-91d8-4735-b3d2-5b7c7eae05df", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration with primary care"}]}, {"id": "ccb34341-c93c-48c3-9ea5-c7e2d50f645c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Long-term services and supports", "description": "LTSS support daily function across home, community, and institutional settings.", "children": [{"id": "2fd58f27-febf-436a-8f58-5778145dda89", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicaid's central role"}, {"id": "790106bd-3429-49ac-b72f-0114bfcd4f3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Home- and community-based services"}, {"id": "cf437d31-3000-4b2a-89d5-09232e59fcf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Nursing facilities and assisted living"}, {"id": "f24e5d66-2fea-4985-ae3b-43c353fd4c62", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility, spend-down, and waiting lists"}]}, {"id": "5940b3a6-7ec5-41c9-ae62-f8c7a16653d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Post-acute care and caregiving", "description": "Transitions and unpaid care are central to outcomes, cost, and equity.", "children": [{"id": "382c6bd4-d707-4be5-b56c-0c07f6c642f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Skilled nursing, rehabilitation, and home health"}, {"id": "84ac0cd7-60d8-4f92-b93d-8e0d67cad64d", "type": "concept", "title": "Hospice and palliative care"}, {"id": "0958fdce-dcc2-4f64-92f9-01ff78621aa2", "type": "concept", "title": "Family caregiver burden"}, {"id": "26a5b0e3-f6a9-45e2-98d0-ec1f505dc31d", "type": "concept", "title": "Care coordination and avoidable readmission"}]}]}, {"id": "91b2a581-a886-47e4-ac78-cbb3cf1c3021", "type": "topic", "title": "Quality, Patient Safety, and System Performance", "description": "Defines quality and safety, examines measurement and accountability, and distinguishes better outcomes from more services or better documentation.", "children": [{"id": "4b9d85bb-7b1f-4315-8eec-a4d2ce283e40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality domains", "description": "Quality includes safety, effectiveness, patient-centeredness, timeliness, efficiency, equity, affordability, and coordination.", "children": [{"id": "f322f42a-9a80-492f-a66b-2ea44d0ca513", "type": "concept", "title": "Structure, process, and outcome"}, {"id": "e1428fae-3db3-4d5d-b4ef-ae2f074211df", "type": "concept", "title": "Clinical and patient-reported measures"}, {"id": "c2bac2b7-5bcb-4a86-b57e-b8b9ed64fb48", "type": "concept", "title": "Population and equity stratification"}, {"id": "f7f77b45-1a78-4436-9263-51d5f918f2eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Benchmarking and risk adjustment"}]}, {"id": "2d742dc0-ff00-41e9-bd4a-646bae674d11", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Patient safety", "description": "Safety science looks beyond individual blame to system design and learning.", "children": [{"id": "f9d35b8e-8ca4-4074-8eab-2662fe0da174", "type": "concept", "title": "Adverse events and near misses"}, {"id": "06d9d057-4235-4643-92f1-127e6c711294", "type": "concept", "title": "Human factors and safety culture"}, {"id": "47fabeab-0705-43a4-a69e-4837b3dc7db1", "type": "concept", "title": "Reporting and root-cause analysis"}, {"id": "7841f1e4-c953-4f1f-8179-2fc3f02216fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Medication, infection, diagnostic, and transition safety"}]}, {"id": "981de314-9f5e-405d-9924-390545d0dccf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accountability and improvement", "description": "Measurement can support learning or create gaming depending on design and incentives.", "children": [{"id": "d0fd2f0b-18dd-4e21-b715-05515a1ec03a", "type": "concept", "title": "Accreditation and public reporting"}, {"id": "05fd79e9-a495-42e0-86a2-640e4fa70fe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Pay for performance"}, {"id": "51d67030-c838-4d69-bec2-af3f6ff18f3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality improvement methods"}, {"id": "b0736656-af07-4b6f-aca2-f1b30f91c32b", "type": "concept", "title": "Unintended consequences and measure burden"}]}]}, {"id": "26ab6c64-846d-441e-832f-1bd8880e432a", "type": "topic", "title": "Access, Disparities, Equity, and Patient Experience", "description": "Investigates coverage, affordability, geography, discrimination, disability, language, immigration, trust, and social conditions as determinants of access and experience.", "children": [{"id": "4778cf8b-57d3-42a3-a89c-e676ed431d48", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dimensions of access", "description": "Coverage is necessary but does not guarantee timely, affordable, acceptable, and reachable care.", "children": [{"id": "3eeacf10-0a77-40f3-9119-6615f223684a", "type": "concept", "title": "Availability and geographic access"}, {"id": "e3d3118d-2e71-440c-aee5-6f7935c37d38", "type": "concept", "title": "Affordability and financial burden"}, {"id": "2f63303f-8c12-4294-beee-a805567c386a", "type": "concept", "title": "Accommodation, language, and disability access"}, {"id": "86043f7a-c609-4b53-bf9c-9864076fb25d", "type": "concept", "title": "Acceptability, trust, and continuity"}]}, {"id": "88bac567-c4ed-4e74-b173-97b83b196e34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Disparities and mechanisms", "description": "Differences reflect policy, institutions, discrimination, resources, exposures, and cumulative disadvantage.", "children": [{"id": "a70c39b7-ea93-47da-aabd-40ee0d2b8c63", "type": "concept", "title": "Race, ethnicity, income, gender, and sexuality"}, {"id": "aa96b7c5-d6bf-4b51-bae9-b2c0900b367e", "type": "concept", "title": "Disability, age, immigration, and language"}, {"id": "144d812d-38cb-40f0-8ef6-7c8fafcd5fc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Rural, urban, and tribal contexts"}, {"id": "a44bab78-9de9-41a5-b03f-ea268ac52705", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural racism and intersectionality"}]}, {"id": "e12b659b-0310-4a3b-b954-5e8cd1fdc386", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Patient experience and financial harm", "description": "System performance includes dignity, communication, navigation, and economic consequences.", "children": [{"id": "25590d54-6273-4de5-8d0f-ba39398c335a", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared decision-making"}, {"id": "e40d8d64-bcb4-48d6-b7cd-61b269955b9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Care coordination and navigation"}, {"id": "b0aa3f9d-1dfd-4ff8-9616-57b28509eaee", "type": "concept", "title": "Medical debt and delayed care"}, {"id": "aa017a77-eaca-439b-b36f-197d97eabc2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Complaints, appeals, and consumer assistance"}]}]}, {"id": "a69d79b5-5301-425d-afc0-ac99e7a26821", "type": "topic", "title": "Public Health, Prevention, and Health Care Integration", "description": "Connects clinical delivery with population health, prevention, emergency preparedness, community partnerships, data exchange, and social-service systems.", "children": [{"id": "4d6556dd-e123-4305-8e1e-652b80cda76e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prevention and population health", "description": "Clinical and public-health systems share responsibility but use different tools and accountability structures.", "children": [{"id": "1797a2ab-8ec7-4526-a4db-396385c80bb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Clinical preventive services"}, {"id": "783a69e5-d9ff-476a-8520-3e36b9183758", "type": "concept", "title": "Population-based prevention"}, {"id": "9c73da35-c73e-4974-aa40-dc2742d2f373", "type": "concept", "title": "Community benefit and community health needs"}, {"id": "b8597756-c6a5-4f42-9e97-0fd8c166f9cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Health-related social needs and upstream policy"}]}, {"id": "07c392b5-9105-456f-8f8d-1d161617179d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public-health infrastructure", "description": "Surveillance, laboratories, preparedness, communication, and community partnerships support system resilience.", "children": [{"id": "6b08bc03-7c4f-4349-a5ba-e92c62a1c3c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal, state, local, tribal, and territorial roles"}, {"id": "c7739034-c129-430c-881e-84dbe88eab60", "type": "concept", "title": "Disease surveillance and reporting"}, {"id": "266c207e-6c5a-459f-9d42-f1d8ffb5011b", "type": "concept", "title": "Emergency preparedness and response"}, {"id": "91ab5843-6668-4ada-adef-ba4f2bf03612", "type": "concept", "title": "Workforce, laboratory, and communication capacity"}]}, {"id": "49d7ce6d-eedd-4d72-b118-4b4f033b8911", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration", "description": "Better population outcomes require aligned data, financing, referral, and accountability.", "children": [{"id": "8bf863c4-3c55-4040-b929-aee25b2fb7a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Health information exchange"}, {"id": "d1a2890e-23b5-4d3d-83ef-bb4548a9adae", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-sector referral and closed-loop systems"}, {"id": "20dbc9a9-b02c-44cb-9898-969fd605f704", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountable communities and place-based partnerships"}, {"id": "d8d31fbf-4061-4ef2-9de3-45c067d8b351", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, and governance"}]}]}, {"id": "5d267496-be38-4b0a-b8c1-d905ada96096", "type": "topic", "title": "Health-System Data, Evidence, and International Comparison", "description": "Builds literacy in national datasets, denominators, trends, benchmarking, and comparisons with peer nations while avoiding simplistic rankings.", "children": [{"id": "22178f55-b663-4c3a-a9bb-c538a7164244", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data sources", "description": "Students learn what major sources measure, who is missing, and which questions each can answer.", "children": [{"id": "26f43c6b-5725-4a44-830d-620257f030b3", "type": "concept", "title": "CMS NHE and enrollment data"}, {"id": "80530e01-f9ed-4a6d-b48e-aa64e6484b53", "type": "concept", "title": "AHRQ MEPS, HCUP, and quality reports"}, {"id": "ae079d58-ce82-4369-a916-2a7816413e83", "type": "concept", "title": "CDC surveys and surveillance"}, {"id": "d2d2f8d1-f950-4cd3-b20c-7bdbe3f83b27", "type": "concept", "title": "Claims, EHR, registry, survey, and qualitative data"}]}, {"id": "6987f4c2-ef09-4e69-b5e3-84125ee63ba6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interpretation", "description": "Health-system claims require careful denominators, time frames, comparators, and causal restraint.", "children": [{"id": "58231dff-7530-400d-b474-4e41d5da27b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Level, rate, share, and growth"}, {"id": "4dfb0997-08bd-4033-9e32-91fe3f605ebc", "type": "concept", "title": "Age and risk adjustment"}, {"id": "88bffc4d-3d4f-4c2f-8026-f6e51fd8f3c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling and administrative-data limits"}, {"id": "964aa5b8-c488-45f8-8ba1-dc9633d75c7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Association versus causation"}]}, {"id": "62d15e7f-0463-488a-b8a4-ba25c4d13d5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "International comparison", "description": "Comparisons clarify design choices when institutions and definitions are kept in context.", "children": [{"id": "4a53e50a-894f-4987-ba24-fd8be1f5c202", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage and benefit entitlement"}, {"id": "ce28543d-e390-49d5-aa5f-09147389b0c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Financing and purchasing"}, {"id": "fdc0693c-c690-41b8-ae53-5c12a4fbd66a", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary care, specialty access, and waiting"}, {"id": "3ea94bb9-6731-4195-9b44-44252841ef8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Spending, outcomes, equity, and patient experience"}]}]}, {"id": "0b3a1664-f2bc-4790-a777-13bcc61b39dd", "type": "topic", "title": "Reform Debates and System Design", "description": "Uses explicit goals and tradeoffs to evaluate coverage expansion, payment reform, competition, regulation, public options, single-payer proposals, and delivery transformation.", "children": [{"id": "9b1c49b1-0ed4-4ae3-9d6d-c9278c407674", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reform objectives", "description": "Proposals should be judged against explicit goals and distributional consequences.", "children": [{"id": "f86bf1e4-5639-4e1e-ae1d-d4b5c4decb9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage and access"}, {"id": "291bade7-bbf1-4624-bccd-092d6f03c5d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Affordability and fiscal sustainability"}, {"id": "c1bef342-ad7b-4339-ba34-2f552ad762f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality, outcomes, and equity"}, {"id": "562dda4a-456b-4b70-9514-77d9e47b45bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Choice, simplicity, resilience, and innovation"}]}, {"id": "c4da5cd1-66a0-43e4-ab67-f03125b442c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy levers", "description": "Reform can change eligibility, financing, prices, payment, organization, regulation, or information.", "children": [{"id": "a18d4db5-2640-4dd7-94cf-ce3fad93d6b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Coverage expansion and public options"}, {"id": "13f8b453-91d3-434b-a965-fc03b52d1ed9", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-payer and multipayer proposals"}, {"id": "9a8e9db2-2b6b-48a8-8d2e-154bc9cd211c", "type": "concept", "title": "Price and market regulation"}, {"id": "75b49f42-aabc-4fdf-873a-9b409b48d411", "type": "concept", "title": "Delivery and payment transformation"}]}, {"id": "e3368a43-8017-4acc-8b5d-71c56acfbab6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feasibility and evaluation", "description": "Good reform analysis addresses authority, administration, stakeholders, transition, and evidence after implementation.", "children": [{"id": "ff7dcf79-1dfe-426d-9d7c-74f538788667", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal and state pathways"}, {"id": "a24e9671-b45e-415b-81a1-d23829116105", "type": "concept", "title": "Budget and financing"}, {"id": "29ca0986-5d89-4c6c-b804-3229e06dd89f", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder power and public opinion"}, {"id": "e54637ad-34db-4a3a-b9bf-28288a6fb076", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation milestones and evaluation measures"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$ushcsjson$::jsonb,
